# Loaded automatically by `next build` (NODE_ENV=production). IN GIT ON PURPOSE.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are COMPILED INTO the JavaScript that every visitor
# downloads. They are public by construction -- this URL is already visible in
# the bundle and in every network request -- so keeping it in the repo leaks
# nothing, and it is the only way the value cannot be forgotten.
#
# It was forgotten. It lived only in .env.local (gitignored, correctly) and in
# the Vercel dashboard, so the 2026-09-26 production build compiled in the
# localhost fallback and the console called http://localhost:8000 from
# adminops.getdaraja.com. Every request failed as a CORS error, which points at
# the allow-list -- the wrong subsystem entirely.
#
# NEVER put a secret in this file. A key, a token, a password, anything that is
# not already public: those belong in the Vercel dashboard, unprefixed, read
# server-side only. Anything named NEXT_PUBLIC_ is shipped to the browser.
NEXT_PUBLIC_DARAJA_API_BASE_URL=https://backendapi.getdaraja.com/dashboard
